<title>BELGIUM: Belgian industrial output down 11.9% yr/yr in Dec.</title>
<headline>Belgian industrial output down 11.9% yr/yr in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian National Statistics Office released the following indices for production in industry excluding the construction sector -</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	    Dec 96     Nov 96	   Dec 95</p>
<p> work day index (1990=100) (*)  96.5	 109.6	    96.1</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) index per working day, adjusted for length and composition of the months  </p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION (FULL YEAR)  1996	  1995</p>
<p>						   99.3	  98.7</p>
<p> SEASONALLY ADJUSTED INDICES(*) Dec 96     Nov 96	   Dec 95</p>
<p> industry as a whole		 94.6	 94.5	     94.8</p>
<p> construction industry	     76.7	 76.2	     79.0</p>
<p> investment goods		    99.7	100.1	    100.5</p>
<p>NOTE - (*) seasonally adjusted based on averages of the last 12 months.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
